{
 "1": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 280\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Timing diagram: four instructions flow through IF, ID, EX, MEM and WB over eight clock cycles, each starting one cycle after the previous one\">\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">Clock cycle</text>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\">\n<text x=\"194\" y=\"30\">1</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"30\">2</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"30\">3</text><text x=\"398\" y=\"30\">4</text><text x=\"466\" y=\"30\">5</text><text x=\"534\" y=\"30\">6</text><text x=\"602\" y=\"30\">7</text><text x=\"670\" y=\"30\">8</text>\n</g>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\">\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"67\">Instr 1</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"113\">Instr 2</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"159\">Instr 3</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"205\">Instr 4</text>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\">\n<rect x=\"163\" y=\"44\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"231\" y=\"44\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"299\" y=\"44\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"367\" y=\"44\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n<rect x=\"231\" y=\"90\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"299\" y=\"90\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"367\" y=\"90\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"435\" y=\"90\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n<rect x=\"299\" y=\"136\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"367\" y=\"136\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"435\" y=\"136\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"503\" y=\"136\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n<rect x=\"367\" y=\"182\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"435\" y=\"182\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"503\" y=\"182\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"571\" y=\"182\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2.5\">\n<rect x=\"435\" y=\"44\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"503\" y=\"90\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"571\" y=\"136\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"639\" y=\"182\" width=\"62\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n</g>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n<text x=\"194\" y=\"67\">IF</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"67\">ID</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"67\">EX</text><text x=\"398\" y=\"67\">MEM</text><text x=\"466\" y=\"67\">WB</text>\n<text x=\"262\" y=\"113\">IF</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"113\">ID</text><text x=\"398\" y=\"113\">EX</text><text x=\"466\" y=\"113\">MEM</text><text x=\"534\" y=\"113\">WB</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"159\">IF</text><text x=\"398\" y=\"159\">ID</text><text x=\"466\" y=\"159\">EX</text><text x=\"534\" y=\"159\">MEM</text><text x=\"602\" y=\"159\">WB</text>\n<text x=\"398\" y=\"205\">IF</text><text x=\"466\" y=\"205\">ID</text><text x=\"534\" y=\"205\">EX</text><text x=\"602\" y=\"205\">MEM</text><text x=\"670\" y=\"205\">WB</text>\n</g>\n<line x1=\"163\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"701\" y2=\"236\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 4\"/>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"262\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\">First result after 5 cycles, then one per cycle: 5 + (4 − 1) = 8 cycles</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.1.1</b> Timing diagram of a five-stage pipeline. Each instruction starts one cycle after the one before it. The green WB boxes show one instruction finishing in every cycle from cycle 5 on, so four instructions need 8 cycles instead of 20.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "2": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 330\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pipelined datapath: PC and instruction memory, IF/ID register, control unit, register file and sign-extend, ID/EX register with EX, M and WB control fields, ALU, EX/MEM register, data memory, MEM/WB register, write-back multiplexer and the path back to the register file\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a52\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"74\" y=\"26\">IF</text><text x=\"252\" y=\"26\">ID</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"26\">EX</text><text x=\"552\" y=\"26\">MEM</text><text x=\"672\" y=\"26\">WB</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"146\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"210\"/><rect x=\"322\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"210\"/><rect x=\"464\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"210\"/><rect x=\"604\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"210\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"322\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"322\" y=\"62\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"322\" y=\"84\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"464\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"464\" y=\"62\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"604\" y=\"40\" width=\"36\" height=\"22\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"340\" y=\"56\">WB</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"78\">M</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"100\">EX</text><text x=\"482\" y=\"56\">WB</text><text x=\"482\" y=\"78\">M</text><text x=\"622\" y=\"56\">WB</text>\n<text x=\"164\" y=\"272\">IF/ID</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"272\">ID/EX</text><text x=\"482\" y=\"272\">EX/MEM</text><text x=\"622\" y=\"272\">MEM/WB</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"14\" y=\"120\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"64\" y=\"95\" width=\"70\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"44\" width=\"120\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"96\" width=\"120\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"200\" width=\"94\" height=\"32\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"372\" y=\"110\" width=\"80\" height=\"70\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"512\" y=\"100\" width=\"80\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"652\" y=\"115\" width=\"40\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"34\" y=\"145\">PC</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"136\">Instr.</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"153\">memory</text><text x=\"252\" y=\"64\">Control</text><text x=\"252\" y=\"145\">Registers</text><text x=\"239\" y=\"221\">Sign-extend</text><text x=\"412\" y=\"150\">ALU</text><text x=\"552\" y=\"141\">Data</text><text x=\"552\" y=\"158\">memory</text><text x=\"672\" y=\"150\">Mux</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#a52)\">\n<path d=\"M54,140 H63\"/><path d=\"M134,140 H145\"/><path d=\"M182,140 H191\"/><path d=\"M182,59 H191\"/><path d=\"M312,59 H321\"/><path d=\"M312,140 H321\"/><path d=\"M286,216 H321\"/><path d=\"M358,145 H371\"/><path d=\"M452,145 H463\"/><path d=\"M500,145 H511\"/><path d=\"M592,145 H603\"/><path d=\"M640,145 H651\"/>\n<path d=\"M358,51 H463\"/><path d=\"M358,73 H463\"/><path d=\"M500,51 H603\"/><path d=\"M358,95 H412 V109\"/><path d=\"M500,73 H552 V99\"/><path d=\"M640,51 H672 V114\"/>\n<path d=\"M672,175 V292 H300 V187\" style=\"stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2.2\"/>\n</g>\n<text x=\"380\" y=\"318\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">Write-back: the result and its destination register number return to the register file</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.2.1</b> The five-stage pipelined datapath (simplified: no branch adder, no multiplexers before the ALU). Blue bars are the pipeline registers; the orange fields on top are control. The control unit fills WB, M and EX in ID; EX is used up in the EX stage, M in MEM, and WB in the last stage, so the control fields shrink from three to two to one. The green path carries the result back to the register file.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "3": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 250\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Forwarding: sub $2 in EX in cycle 3; its result is forwarded from EX/MEM to the and instruction's EX in cycle 4 and from MEM/WB to the or instruction's EX in cycle 5\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a531\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\"><text x=\"218\" y=\"30\">1</text><text x=\"294\" y=\"30\">2</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"30\">3</text><text x=\"446\" y=\"30\">4</text><text x=\"522\" y=\"30\">5</text><text x=\"598\" y=\"30\">6</text><text x=\"674\" y=\"30\">7</text></g>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"end\"><text x=\"170\" y=\"30\">Cycle</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"73\">sub $2, $1, $3</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"133\">and $12, $2, $5</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"193\">or $13, $6, $2</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\">\n<rect x=\"183\" y=\"50\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"259\" y=\"50\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"411\" y=\"50\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"487\" y=\"50\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n<rect x=\"259\" y=\"110\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"335\" y=\"110\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"487\" y=\"110\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"563\" y=\"110\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n<rect x=\"335\" y=\"170\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"411\" y=\"170\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"563\" y=\"170\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"639\" y=\"170\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/>\n</g>\n<rect x=\"335\" y=\"50\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2.5\"><rect x=\"411\" y=\"110\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"487\" y=\"170\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n<text x=\"218\" y=\"73\">IF</text><text x=\"294\" y=\"73\">ID</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"73\">EX</text><text x=\"446\" y=\"73\">MEM</text><text x=\"522\" y=\"73\">WB</text>\n<text x=\"294\" y=\"133\">IF</text><text x=\"370\" y=\"133\">ID</text><text x=\"446\" y=\"133\">EX</text><text x=\"522\" y=\"133\">MEM</text><text x=\"598\" y=\"133\">WB</text>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"193\">IF</text><text x=\"446\" y=\"193\">ID</text><text x=\"522\" y=\"193\">EX</text><text x=\"598\" y=\"193\">MEM</text><text x=\"674\" y=\"193\">WB</text>\n</g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#a531)\"><path d=\"M408,86 V108\"/><path d=\"M484,86 V168\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\"><text x=\"396\" y=\"103\" text-anchor=\"end\">from EX/MEM</text><text x=\"492\" y=\"163\">from MEM/WB</text></g>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"236\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">$2 = 30 − 12 = 18 exists at the end of cycle 3; the register file gets it only in cycle 5</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.3.1</b> Forwarding paths. The orange box makes $2; the green boxes need it. Each arrow points down and to the right, forward in time, so forwarding works: <code>and</code> takes $2 from EX/MEM at the start of cycle 4, <code>or</code> takes it from MEM/WB at the start of cycle 5. No stall is needed.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "4": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 280\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two-bit branch predictor: four states, strongly taken 11, weakly taken 10, weakly not taken 01 and strongly not taken 00; a not-taken outcome moves one state right, a taken outcome moves one state left\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a541\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs>\n<text x=\"16\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">T = branch taken, N = not taken</text>\n<g style=\"stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"32\" y=\"110\" width=\"140\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next)\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"110\" width=\"140\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next)\"/><rect x=\"376\" y=\"110\" width=\"140\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live)\"/><rect x=\"548\" y=\"110\" width=\"140\" height=\"64\" rx=\"10\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live)\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"137\" font-weight=\"600\">Strongly taken</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"157\">11: predict T</text><text x=\"274\" y=\"137\" font-weight=\"600\">Weakly taken</text><text x=\"274\" y=\"157\">10: predict T</text><text x=\"446\" y=\"137\" font-weight=\"600\">Weakly not taken</text><text x=\"446\" y=\"157\">01: predict N</text><text x=\"618\" y=\"137\" font-weight=\"600\">Strongly not taken</text><text x=\"618\" y=\"157\">00: predict N</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:2\" marker-end=\"url(#a541)\">\n<path d=\"M142,110 Q188,40 234,110\"/><path d=\"M314,110 Q360,40 406,110\"/><path d=\"M486,110 Q532,40 578,110\"/>\n<path d=\"M234,174 Q188,244 142,174\"/><path d=\"M406,174 Q360,244 314,174\"/><path d=\"M578,174 Q532,244 486,174\"/>\n<path d=\"M52,110 C42,60 102,60 92,110\"/><path d=\"M628,110 C618,60 678,60 668,110\"/>\n</g>\n<g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"188\" y=\"66\">N</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"66\">N</text><text x=\"532\" y=\"66\">N</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"232\">T</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"232\">T</text><text x=\"532\" y=\"232\">T</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"62\">T</text><text x=\"648\" y=\"62\">N</text></g>\n<line x1=\"360\" y1=\"246\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"270\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 4\"/>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"188\" y=\"264\">predicts taken</text><text x=\"532\" y=\"264\">predicts not taken</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.4.1</b> The 2-bit saturating-counter predictor. A not-taken outcome (N) moves one state right; a taken outcome (T) moves one state left; the end states stay put. From a strong state, one surprise only weakens the guess, so a loop branch that exits once is still predicted taken on re-entry.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "5": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 320\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pipeline in cycle 6 when add overflows in EX: lw in IF, slt in ID and add in EX are flushed; or in MEM and and in WB complete; EPC gets 4C hex, Cause gets 12 and the PC gets 8000 0180 hex\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a551\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"38\">IF</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"38\">ID</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"38\">EX</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"38\">MEM</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"38\">WB</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"50\" width=\"128\" height=\"62\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"156\" y=\"50\" width=\"128\" height=\"62\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"436\" y=\"50\" width=\"128\" height=\"62\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"576\" y=\"50\" width=\"128\" height=\"62\" rx=\"8\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"296\" y=\"50\" width=\"128\" height=\"62\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"76\">lw $16, 50($7)</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"98\">at 54 hex</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"76\">slt $15, $6, $7</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"98\">at 50 hex</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"76\">add $1, $2, $1</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"98\">at 4C: overflow</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"76\">or $13, $2, $6</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"98\">at 48 hex</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"76\">and $12, $2, $5</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"98\">at 44 hex</text></g>\n<g style=\"stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"36\" y=\"124\" width=\"88\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live)\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"124\" width=\"88\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live)\"/><rect x=\"316\" y=\"124\" width=\"88\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live)\"/><rect x=\"452\" y=\"124\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next)\"/><rect x=\"592\" y=\"124\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next)\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"142\">flushed</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"142\">flushed</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"142\">flushed</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"142\">completes</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"142\">completes</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"60\" y=\"214\" width=\"180\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"214\" width=\"180\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"480\" y=\"214\" width=\"180\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"150\" y=\"236\" font-weight=\"600\">EPC</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"257\">0000 004C hex</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"236\" font-weight=\"600\">Cause</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"257\">12 (overflow)</text><text x=\"570\" y=\"236\" font-weight=\"600\">PC</text><text x=\"570\" y=\"257\">8000 0180 hex</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\" marker-end=\"url(#a551)\"><path d=\"M340,152 L170,212\"/><path d=\"M360,152 V212\"/><path d=\"M380,152 L550,212\"/></g>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"302\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\">Cycle 7: the first handler instruction is fetched from 8000 0180 hex</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.5.1</b> The pipeline in cycle 6, when <code>add</code> overflows in EX. Instructions are drawn in pipeline order, youngest on the left. The two older instructions on the right complete; the faulting one and the two younger ones are flushed. The hardware then fills EPC, Cause and PC.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "6": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 320\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Dynamically scheduled superscalar pipeline: in-order fetch and decode unit, four reservation stations, four functional units (two integer, floating point, load/store), and an in-order commit unit with reorder buffer\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a561\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"150\" y=\"18\" width=\"420\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"256\" width=\"420\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"150\" y=\"96\" width=\"96\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"96\" width=\"96\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"366\" y=\"96\" width=\"96\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"474\" y=\"96\" width=\"96\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"150\" y=\"164\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"164\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"366\" y=\"164\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"474\" y=\"164\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"360\" y=\"45\">Instruction fetch and decode unit</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"283\">Commit unit with reorder buffer</text>\n<text x=\"198\" y=\"121\">RS</text><text x=\"306\" y=\"121\">RS</text><text x=\"414\" y=\"121\">RS</text><text x=\"522\" y=\"121\">RS</text>\n<text x=\"198\" y=\"191\">Integer</text><text x=\"306\" y=\"191\">Integer</text><text x=\"414\" y=\"191\">FP</text><text x=\"522\" y=\"191\">Load/store</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#a561)\">\n<path d=\"M198,62 V94\"/><path d=\"M306,62 V94\"/><path d=\"M414,62 V94\"/><path d=\"M522,62 V94\"/>\n<path d=\"M198,136 V162\"/><path d=\"M306,136 V162\"/><path d=\"M414,136 V162\"/><path d=\"M522,136 V162\"/>\n<path d=\"M198,208 V254\"/><path d=\"M306,208 V254\"/><path d=\"M414,208 V254\"/><path d=\"M522,208 V254\"/>\n</g>\n<path d=\"M570,232 H600 V116 H572\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#a561)\"/>\n<line x1=\"150\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"570\" y2=\"232\" style=\"stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:6 4\"/>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\"><text x=\"16\" y=\"45\">In-order issue</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"146\">Out-of-order</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"164\">execute</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"283\">In-order commit</text>\n<text x=\"610\" y=\"160\">results to</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"178\">waiting RS</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.6.1</b> A dynamically scheduled superscalar pipeline. Instructions enter in program order, wait in reservation stations (RS) until their operands arrive, execute in any order on the functional units, and are committed in program order by the reorder buffer. The dashed green result bus carries each result to every station waiting for it.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "7": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"SIMD versus MIMD: on the left one control unit broadcasts one instruction to four processing elements, each with its own memory; on the right four cores, each with its own control and cache, share memory through an interconnect\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a571\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"180\" y=\"28\">SIMD</text><text x=\"540\" y=\"28\">MIMD</text></g>\n<line x1=\"360\" y1=\"14\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"296\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5;stroke-dasharray:5 4\"/>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"42\" width=\"140\" height=\"40\" rx=\"6\" style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"/>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"currentColor\">Control unit</text>\n<path d=\"M180,82 V106 M56,106 H304\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\" marker-end=\"url(#a571)\"><path d=\"M56,106 V124\"/><path d=\"M139,106 V124\"/><path d=\"M222,106 V124\"/><path d=\"M304,106 V124\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"24\" y=\"126\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"107\" y=\"126\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"126\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"272\" y=\"126\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"24\" y=\"196\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"107\" y=\"196\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"196\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"272\" y=\"196\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\"/></g>\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:2\"><line x1=\"56\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"56\" y2=\"196\"/><line x1=\"139\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"139\" y2=\"196\"/><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"196\"/><line x1=\"304\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"196\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"56\" y=\"151\">PE 1</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"151\">PE 2</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"151\">PE 3</text><text x=\"304\" y=\"151\">PE 4</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"221\">Mem 1</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"221\">Mem 2</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"221\">Mem 3</text><text x=\"304\" y=\"221\">Mem 4</text>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"270\">1 instruction stream,</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"288\">4 data streams</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"384\" y=\"46\" width=\"64\" height=\"44\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"467\" y=\"46\" width=\"64\" height=\"44\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"550\" y=\"46\" width=\"64\" height=\"44\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"632\" y=\"46\" width=\"64\" height=\"44\" rx=\"5\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"384\" y=\"100\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"467\" y=\"100\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"550\" y=\"100\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"632\" y=\"100\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"384\" y=\"160\" width=\"312\" height=\"32\" rx=\"6\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"460\" y=\"216\" width=\"160\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"/>\n<g style=\"stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:2\"><line x1=\"416\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"416\" y2=\"160\"/><line x1=\"499\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"499\" y2=\"160\"/><line x1=\"582\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"582\" y2=\"160\"/><line x1=\"664\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"664\" y2=\"160\"/><line x1=\"540\" y1=\"192\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"216\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"416\" y=\"73\">Core 1</text><text x=\"499\" y=\"73\">Core 2</text><text x=\"582\" y=\"73\">Core 3</text><text x=\"664\" y=\"73\">Core 4</text><text x=\"416\" y=\"120\">Cache</text><text x=\"499\" y=\"120\">Cache</text><text x=\"582\" y=\"120\">Cache</text><text x=\"664\" y=\"120\">Cache</text>\n<text x=\"540\" y=\"181\">Interconnect (bus or network)</text><text x=\"540\" y=\"238\">Shared memory</text>\n<text x=\"540\" y=\"270\">4 instruction streams,</text><text x=\"540\" y=\"288\">4 data streams</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.7.1</b> SIMD and MIMD side by side. In SIMD (left) one control unit (orange) broadcasts the same instruction to four processing elements, each working on its own memory. In MIMD (right) every core has its own control and runs its own program; here they share memory through an interconnect. Replace the shared memory by private memories and a network and you have a cluster.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "8": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 320\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Vector processor: main memory connects to a pipelined vector load/store unit, which connects to eight vector registers of 64 elements; the registers feed a four-stage floating-point multiply pipeline and a four-stage add pipeline; results return to the registers and the multiply output is chained into the add pipeline\">\n<defs><marker id=\"a581\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker><marker id=\"a582\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" style=\"fill:var(--live)\"/></marker></defs>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"130\" width=\"120\" height=\"64\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"168\" y=\"130\" width=\"132\" height=\"64\" rx=\"6\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"240\" rx=\"4\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M340,80 H460 M340,110 H460 M340,140 H460 M340,170 H460 M340,200 H460 M340,230 H460 M340,260 H460\" style=\"stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"500\" y=\"66\" width=\"160\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"500\" y=\"170\" width=\"160\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M540,66 V106 M580,66 V106 M620,66 V106 M540,170 V210 M580,170 V210 M620,170 V210\" style=\"stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:1.5\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--bg);stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"236\" width=\"120\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"168\" y=\"236\" width=\"60\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"236\" width=\"60\" height=\"34\" rx=\"5\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"76\" y=\"158\">Main</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"177\">memory</text><text x=\"234\" y=\"158\">Vector</text><text x=\"234\" y=\"177\">load/store</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"70\">V0</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"100\">V1</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"130\">V2</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"160\">V3</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"190\">V4</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"220\">V5</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"250\">V6</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"280\">V7</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"38\">Vector registers, 64 elements each</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"56\">FP multiply pipeline</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"230\">FP add pipeline</text>\n<text x=\"76\" y=\"258\">Scalar regs</text><text x=\"198\" y=\"258\">VLR</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"258\">Mask</text><text x=\"575\" y=\"270\">results written back</text><text x=\"566\" y=\"158\">chaining</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:2\" marker-end=\"url(#a581)\"><path d=\"M136,152 H166\"/><path d=\"M168,174 H138\"/><path d=\"M300,152 H338\"/><path d=\"M340,174 H302\"/><path d=\"M460,86 H498\"/><path d=\"M460,196 H498\"/><path d=\"M660,86 H690 V250 H462\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M660,190 H690\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:2\"/>\n<path d=\"M640,106 V136 H486 V182 H498\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-dasharray:6 4\" marker-end=\"url(#a582)\"/>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.8.1</b> A vector processor in the style of VMIPS. Each functional unit is a pipeline (the four boxes inside each green unit are stages), so once full it delivers one result per cycle. The dashed orange path is <b>chaining</b>: products leave the multiplier and enter the adder element by element, without waiting for the whole vector to be written. VLR sets the vector length and Mask switches elements off.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
 "9": "<figure class=\"fig\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 250\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Issue slots used by threads A, B and C over four cycles on a four-issue core: superscalar alone uses 3 of 16 slots, coarse multithreading 7, fine multithreading 8 and simultaneous multithreading 15\">\n<g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"40\">Superscalar</text><text x=\"272\" y=\"40\">Coarse MT</text><text x=\"444\" y=\"40\">Fine MT</text><text x=\"616\" y=\"40\">SMT</text></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--line2);stroke-width:1.5\"><rect x=\"32\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"128\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"128\"/><rect x=\"376\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"128\"/><rect x=\"548\" y=\"56\" width=\"136\" height=\"128\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M66,56 V184 M100,56 V184 M134,56 V184 M32,88 H168 M32,120 H168 M32,152 H168 M238,56 V184 M272,56 V184 M306,56 V184 M204,88 H340 M204,120 H340 M204,152 H340 M410,56 V184 M444,56 V184 M478,56 V184 M376,88 H512 M376,120 H512 M376,152 H512 M582,56 V184 M616,56 V184 M650,56 V184 M548,88 H684 M548,120 H684 M548,152 H684\" style=\"stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1\"/>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--accent-soft);stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"34\" y=\"58\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"154\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"206\" y=\"58\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"378\" y=\"58\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"550\" y=\"58\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"550\" y=\"154\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"378\" y=\"154\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--live-soft);stroke:var(--live);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"206\" y=\"122\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"206\" y=\"154\" width=\"98\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"378\" y=\"90\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"58\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"550\" y=\"90\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"550\" y=\"122\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"584\" y=\"154\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/></g>\n<g style=\"fill:var(--next-soft);stroke:var(--next);stroke-width:2\"><rect x=\"378\" y=\"122\" width=\"98\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"652\" y=\"58\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"90\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"584\" y=\"122\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"652\" y=\"154\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" rx=\"4\"/></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"66\" y=\"77\">A</text><text x=\"49\" y=\"173\">A</text><text x=\"238\" y=\"77\">A</text><text x=\"238\" y=\"141\">B</text><text x=\"255\" y=\"173\">B</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"77\">A</text><text x=\"410\" y=\"109\">B</text><text x=\"427\" y=\"141\">C</text><text x=\"393\" y=\"173\">A</text><text x=\"582\" y=\"77\">A</text><text x=\"633\" y=\"77\">B</text><text x=\"667\" y=\"77\">C</text><text x=\"582\" y=\"109\">B</text><text x=\"650\" y=\"109\">C</text><text x=\"565\" y=\"141\">B</text><text x=\"616\" y=\"141\">C</text><text x=\"565\" y=\"173\">A</text><text x=\"616\" y=\"173\">B</text><text x=\"667\" y=\"173\">C</text></g>\n<g font-size=\"13\" fill=\"currentColor\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"206\">3 of 16 slots</text><text x=\"272\" y=\"206\">7 of 16 slots</text><text x=\"444\" y=\"206\">8 of 16 slots</text><text x=\"616\" y=\"206\">15 of 16 slots</text>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"236\">Columns: 4 issue slots. Rows: clock cycles 1 to 4, time runs down.</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 5.9.1</b> How four ways of running threads A (blue), B (orange) and C (green) fill the issue slots of a four-issue core. Thread A misses in the cache in cycles 2 and 3. Alone, the core wastes 13 of 16 slots. Coarse MT switches to B after a one-cycle refill; fine MT gives each cycle to the next ready thread, and A is ready again in cycle 4; SMT mixes threads inside a cycle and wastes only one slot.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
